export const bundledPosts = {"building-in-public-with-ai-agents":{"zh":"---\ntitle: \"从折腾软件开始\"\ndescription: \"为什么我会持续探索 Web coding、AI Agent、自动化和企业知识，以及这个网站接下来会记录什么。\"\npublishedAt: \"2026-08-09T01:00:00.000Z\"\n---\n\n我一直很喜欢折腾软件。\n\n不是为了追每一个新工具，而是想知道：一件原本需要人反复操作的事情，能不能被重新组织，最后变成一个可靠、可以一直运行的系统。\n\n过去，这种想法经常停在原型。开发、维护和整合的成本太高，一个人很难把所有环节都做完整。AI Agent 改变了这条边界。它没有让判断和维护消失，却明显放大了一个人把想法变成软件的能力。\n\n## 我正在探索什么\n\n我目前在 [UChat](https://uchat.au) 担任首席营销官，也在构建 [FengTalk.ai](https://fengtalk.ai)。这些工作虽然形态不同，但都围绕几个相互连接的问题：\n\n- Web coding 如何让想法更快变成真正可用的产品\n- AI Agent 如何理解目标，并在边界内持续完成工作\n- outreach 如何从零散动作变成可以观察和改进的流程\n- company knowledge 如何被整理成团队和 Agent 都能使用的上下文\n- 自动化如何接管重复劳动，同时把关键判断留给人\n\n我关心的不只是“能不能跑起来”。一个系统是否可靠、信息是否清楚、失败时能否恢复，以及它是否真的适合业务，往往比第一次演示更重要。\n\n## 为什么写下来\n\n很多 AI 内容停留在产品发布、功能罗列和短暂的新鲜感。我更想记录实际构建过程中发生的事情：做过哪些选择，哪些方案失败了，怎样验证，以及最后为什么保留现在这个版本。\n\n这个网站会主要围绕 Web coding、AI Agent、自动化、outreach、外贸业务和企业知识展开。有时是一篇完整教程，有时是一次产品复盘，也可能只是一个值得继续验证的小发现。\n\n## 从这里开始\n\n第一版网站本身就是一次公开实践：保留一套成熟个人网站的完整设计与交互，同时重建身份、内容、部署和后续维护流程，并让 AI Agent 能够安全地帮助更新博客。\n\n我希望这里最终不只是文章的集合，而是一份长期积累的工作记录。哪些东西真的有用，时间会给出答案。\n\n","en":"---\ntitle: \"It Started With Tinkering\"\ndescription: \"Why I keep exploring web coding, AI agents, automation, and company knowledge—and what I plan to document here.\"\n---\n\nI have always liked tinkering with software.\n\nNot because I want to chase every new tool, but because I keep returning to one question: can something that requires repeated manual work be reorganized into a dependable system that keeps running?\n\nIn the past, that question often ended with a prototype. Development, maintenance, and integration were expensive, and one person could rarely carry every part to completion. AI agents have moved that boundary. They have not removed judgment or maintenance, but they have dramatically amplified one person’s ability to turn an idea into software.\n\n## What I am exploring\n\nI currently serve as Chief Marketing Officer at [UChat](https://uchat.au), while building [FengTalk.ai](https://fengtalk.ai). The work takes different forms, but it keeps circling a connected set of questions:\n\n- How web coding can turn an idea into a useful product faster\n- How AI agents can understand a goal and keep working within clear boundaries\n- How outreach can become an observable, improvable system instead of scattered activity\n- How company knowledge can become context that both teams and agents can use\n- How automation can take repetitive work while leaving consequential judgment to people\n\nI care about more than whether something runs once. Reliability, clarity, recovery, and fit with the actual business usually matter more than the first demo.\n\n## Why write it down\n\nMuch of the conversation around AI stops at product launches, feature lists, and temporary novelty. I want to document what happens while building: the choices, the failed approaches, the validation, and the reasons the current version survived.\n\nThis site will focus on web coding, AI agents, automation, outreach, international business, and company knowledge. Sometimes that will mean a complete tutorial. Sometimes it will be a product retrospective or a small observation that deserves a longer test.\n\n## Starting here\n\nThe first version of this site is itself a public experiment: preserve the complete design and interaction of a mature personal site while rebuilding its identity, content, deployment, and maintenance workflow—and make it safe for an AI agent to help publish future writing.\n\nI hope this becomes more than a collection of posts. I want it to become a durable record of the work. Time will tell which ideas were genuinely useful.\n\n"}} as const
export const bundledNewsletters = {"1":{"zh":"---\ntitle: \"FengTalk 月度更新 01\"\ndescription: \"关于 Web coding、AI Agent、自动化和正在构建的产品。\"\n---\n\n欢迎来到第一期归档。\n\n这里会收录我近期在 Web coding、AI Agent、自动化、outreach 和企业知识方面的实践，也会整理新文章、产品进展以及值得继续验证的想法。\n\nNewsletter 的正式订阅还没有开放。在邮件服务和隐私流程准备完成前，这个页面只作为公开归档，不会收集邮箱。\n\n你可以先阅读[从折腾软件开始](/blog/building-in-public-with-ai-agents)，或者通过 [hi@fengtalk.ai](mailto:hi@fengtalk.ai) 联系我。\n\n","en":"---\ntitle: \"FengTalk Monthly Update 01\"\ndescription: \"Web coding, AI agents, automation, and the products currently being built.\"\n---\n\nWelcome to the first archived update.\n\nThis is where I will collect recent work in web coding, AI agents, automation, outreach, and company knowledge, alongside new writing, product progress, and ideas worth testing further.\n\nThe newsletter is not open for subscription yet. Until the email service and privacy workflow are ready, this page remains a public archive and does not collect addresses.\n\nStart with [It Started With Tinkering](/en/blog/building-in-public-with-ai-agents), or reach me at [hi@fengtalk.ai](mailto:hi@fengtalk.ai).\n\n"}} as const
